      },
      "col2": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
        "largeheadline": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "lee.fuller1@stryker.com",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "lee.fuller1@stryker.com",
          "jcr:created": "Wed Aug 01 2018 19:54:42 GMT-0400",
          "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
          "line1": "<span class=\"urw-egyptienne\"><span class=\"fontsize-2-5-vw\">Dedicated to<br>\r\n <span class=\"futura-bold\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255,181,0);\">improving </span>outcomes</span></span></span>",
          "line2": "<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Published literature has long confirmed the significant social and economic burden associated with postoperative complications. More than 180 peer-reviewed medical journals have supported the use of SPY technology. Many of these studies have demonstrated an improvement in patient outcomes and a reduction in hospital costs as a result of SPY technology.<sup>2</sup> In fact, the PILLAR II trial found that the use of SPY technology may assist in surgical decision making, which may reduce the occurrence of costly complications.<sup>3</sup><br>\r\n</p>\r\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Thu Aug 02 2018 14:57:05 GMT-0400",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/largeheadline",
          "backgroundColor": "rgba(255,255,255,1)",
          "textIsRich": [
            "true",
            "true"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
